WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.480
- I had some health issues when
I was younger with my heart.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.550
I am grateful many mornings I wake up.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.383
I say this to people all the time,

00:00:06.383 --> 00:00:08.410
I've been happy rich and
I've been happy poor.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.880
Happy rich is better.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.060
Successful people and wealthy people

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.270
have a subtle distinction.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.103
They don't look at price.

00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:15.103
They look at worth.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.370
- Need motivation?

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.430
- Watch a top 10 with Believe Nation.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.521
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:26.730
I believe in you and
this channel is designed

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.480
to be a part of your
daily success routine.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.650
So let's get your motivation to a 10

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.590
and get you believing in you.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.280
Grab a snack and chew on today's lessons

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.903
from a man who went from being
born in a middle class family

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:40.050
to building one of the most successful

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.152
financial services company in the world.

00:00:42.152 --> 00:00:45.470
And be one of the top motivational
speakers on the planet.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.110
He's Ed Mylett and here's my take

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:50.307
on his top 10 rules to success volume two.

00:00:50.307 --> 00:00:52.890
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.950
Okay let's kick it off with
rule number one, grow you.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.530
- I don't believe in
faking it 'til you make it.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.930
Because you know what
entrepreneurialism is right?

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.770
It's the greatest self-discovery process

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.330
in the history of mankind.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.163
Isn't it?

00:01:11.163 --> 00:01:12.090
You learn more about yourself.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.441
What you don't know, your
resiliency, how tough you are,

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.780
what your weaknesses are,
by being an entrepreneur.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.770
It's probably the greatest
self-discovery program

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:19.603
in the history of the world.

00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:22.230
It's also this, it's the
greatest self-improvement program

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.580
with the highest compensation
package possibly attached

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.622
to it too.

00:01:25.622 --> 00:01:28.260
Entrepreneurism is a
self-improvement program

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.400
with massive compensation
package attached to it.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.980
And that's why too many
of you are too focused

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.200
on growing your company

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.100
and not focused enough on growing you.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.060
Because your company will
never ever exceed your identity

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.700
or your vision for it.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.533
You got to grow you

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:43.660
because what'll happen
when it starts to grow,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.110
you'll start making unconscious
mistakes to shrink it.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.870
Making bad calls, getting weak,

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.390
getting lazy, making mistakes.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.320
You're all nodding because
you've all done it,

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.340
because at some point your
business got ahead of you.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.670
It will never exceed your
identity and your vision.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.440
Because if the company
catches your vision,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.730
the company catches your
identity, you're dying.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:04.100
- Rule number two, be
in a state of gratitude.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.460
- I'm grateful that I have the money

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.880
for the plane tickets still.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.770
- Right.
- It's odd how small things,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.320
I love big things, I love having my jet,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.570
but I make sure that I'm grateful for what

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.990
most people will think are small things.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:16.990
And I really am.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.880
I had some health issues when
I was younger with my heart.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.070
I am grateful many mornings I wake up.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:26.320
My day starts with gratitude,
I'm awake many, many mornings.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.695
And so that's a center piece of my life.

00:02:28.695 --> 00:02:31.070
It's odd because I have
all these things in my head

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.039
from when I was a kid,

00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:33.960
gratitude is sort of the antidote

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.830
for everything not good in my life.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.525
- Rule number three, care about people.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.353
- What would you say is
your greatest asset, skill?

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.540
- I love people, man.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.710
I care about people, I sincerely do.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:53.113
And so, whether that's, yeah,
I mean I want to help you.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.870
People say, how do you get back

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.170
to all these people on social media?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.186
I care, you know.
- Yeah, it's a lot, yeah.

00:02:59.186 --> 00:03:01.244
- You and I have talked about that fact.

00:03:01.244 --> 00:03:04.249
My intent is good, man.

00:03:04.249 --> 00:03:07.010
I want to make a difference in the world.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.338
We're all put here for a reason.

00:03:08.338 --> 00:03:10.266
It sounds hokie.

00:03:10.266 --> 00:03:11.890
I've made a lot of money.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.430
I'd like to make more
money but it's not really

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.263
a driver for me.

00:03:14.263 --> 00:03:15.096
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:03:15.096 --> 00:03:15.929
You've got a bunch of homes.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.881
- I've filled that need.

00:03:16.881 --> 00:03:18.750
It's not long lasting.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.830
No material thing I've
ever required was as cool

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.960
as I thought it would be.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.070
It's cool.
- It's cool for a week or two.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.903
- Exactly.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:25.736
- And then you're like now what?

00:03:25.736 --> 00:03:26.569
- Now what, right?

00:03:26.569 --> 00:03:27.402
It's empty.

00:03:27.402 --> 00:03:29.210
By the way, I think
everybody should have a jet

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.043
if they can have one.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.520
Everybody ought to have
unicorn in their waterfall.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.990
Everybody ought to live oceanfront.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.740
I say this to people all the time,

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.890
I've been happy rich and
I've been happy poor.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.260
Happy rich is better.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.070
Don't let anybody tell you
happy rich ain't better

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:41.903
than happy poor.

00:03:41.903 --> 00:03:42.736
Trust me.

00:03:42.736 --> 00:03:43.569
It's better.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:44.840
And money's a magnifier.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.290
If you're a really good person.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.310
You get a bunch of money.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.070
It's probably going to
magnify your generosity

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.690
and your kindness and your patience.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.250
And if you're a curmudgeon
and mean and hurt people

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.546
money's going to magnify that too.

00:03:54.546 --> 00:03:56.390
So I'd rather have a bunch of money.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.223
Hands down.

00:03:57.223 --> 00:03:58.056
Right?

00:03:58.056 --> 00:03:59.490
But it's not something that drives me

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.323
in my life.

00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:01.800
It doesn't fulfill me.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.380
- Rule number four, stop
negotiating the price.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.680
- When I was poor, everywhere I went

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.640
I flipped the price tag over.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.473
What's it cost?

00:04:09.473 --> 00:04:10.306
What's it cost?

00:04:10.306 --> 00:04:11.139
What's it cost?

00:04:11.139 --> 00:04:11.972
What's it cost?

00:04:11.972 --> 00:04:14.100
I was constantly negotiating
the price for everything

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:14.933
in my life.

00:04:14.933 --> 00:04:17.120
You do that when you come
from a place of scarcity,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.340
of being poor.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.530
Successful people and wealthy people

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.770
have a subtle distinction.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:22.603
They don't look at price.

00:04:22.603 --> 00:04:24.210
They look at worth.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.850
Is this worth it?

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.940
If you're constantly
looking at the price tag,

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.510
you'll eventually relent.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.850
You'll eventually give in.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.170
Stop negotiating the price.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.120
It's a freeing experience
to totally commit.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.800
When you totally commit to a relationship,

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.760
to a business, to your
fitness, to your faith.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.730
It's a freeing powerful.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.830
It's almost like removing kryptonite

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.990
from your life, when you totally commit.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.200
Can you do that?

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.700
The people around you, always
say it's costing too much,

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.000
it's costing too much.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.074
And you're going, maybe
it's costing too much.

00:04:55.074 --> 00:04:58.100
You've got to start
going, no, it's worth it.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.220
It's not the price, it's the worth.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.350
It's a subtle distinction in your life.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.060
- Rule number five, have persistence.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.120
- You've been very successful
as an entrepreneur.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.863
Have you always been successful?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.832
- You just said the word
entrepreneur and always successful.

00:05:12.832 --> 00:05:15.080
- Thank you, listen to him.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.685
I try to tell everybody this.

00:05:16.685 --> 00:05:17.890
Nobody listens to me.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.860
I've haven't met one
entrepreneur that's like oh yeah,

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.620
everything I have ever done works.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:22.453
- Come on, bro.

00:05:22.453 --> 00:05:23.286
- And they're lying if they tell you that.

00:05:23.286 --> 00:05:24.119
- Well they're not an entrepreneur.

00:05:24.119 --> 00:05:25.740
They've inherited
something or I don't know.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:26.746
- Right, mostly inherited.

00:05:26.746 --> 00:05:27.579
- Right.

00:05:27.579 --> 00:05:29.210
Because if you're an
entrepreneur, you have not always

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.590
been successful, right?

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.910
- From Steve Jobs down.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:32.743
- All the way.

00:05:32.743 --> 00:05:36.180
And so I've had successes
and then I'll go backwards.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.160
Like most entrepreneurs,
there's false start after

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.210
false start after false start.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.860
So I would get it going and
then it would go backwards.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.400
I'd save some money, then I'd blow it.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.003
My business would grow,
then it would shrink.

00:05:44.003 --> 00:05:47.040
No, I've had tons of different financial

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:47.900
events happen in my life.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.670
And actually after people
thought I was pretty successful,

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.690
I'd become a millionaire,
about 26 years old.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.523
I'd become a millionaire.

00:05:54.523 --> 00:05:56.710
I was making a million
dollars a year and I ended up

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.543
losing it all.

00:05:57.543 --> 00:05:59.830
It ended up, I lost a home, I lost a car.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.610
I ended up moving into an apartment.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.320
I was newly married and
I'll never forget this.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.680
I remember because this ocean's out there.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.400
We're looking at it right now.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.920
I remember honestly, a defining moment.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.700
I had everything turned off.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.290
You can have power turned
off and still survive.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.520
One thing I learned, you don't
want your water turned off.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.840
And we have the water cut off.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:16.760
- With your newlywed.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:17.593
- My newlywed.

00:06:17.593 --> 00:06:18.426
Six weeks married.

00:06:18.426 --> 00:06:19.259
- Is she still with you?

00:06:19.259 --> 00:06:20.092
- She's still with me.

00:06:20.092 --> 00:06:20.960
She's floating around here somewhere.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:21.930
- That's it man.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:22.824
- She's with me.

00:06:22.824 --> 00:06:23.657
- We've got so much in common.

00:06:23.657 --> 00:06:24.490
- I know we do.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.390
Both high school and the
same thing with our wives.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.380
And long story short, we
had to go every morning

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.700
out of the apartment, go down to the pool

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.090
and shower outdoors.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.250
And we'd bring our toothbrush.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.690
It was just shameful for me.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.480
- Rule number six, keep the
promises you made to you.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.332
- The key to self-confidence
is really simple.

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:43.990
This is absolutely, I've
trained hundreds of thousands

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:45.730
of people, I've spoken to millions

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.020
of people around the world.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.910
I can tell you this, the
self-confident people I know,

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:52.370
whether they are athletes,
school teachers, mechanics,

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.610
parents, stay-at-home moms,
you name it, they have

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:58.560
a pattern of keeping promises
they make to themselves.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.730
The ground work of beginning
to build self-confidence

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.620
is to begin to keep the
promises you make to you

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.020
and that's why it's important to begin

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.100
to even make small promises.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.150
If you're going to get up at
a certain time in the morning,

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.440
not only do it but then
give yourself credit.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.000
Say, I did what I said I was going to do.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.770
If it's in your diet or your fitness,

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:17.080
don't just eat the healthy
foods, go, I'm doing what

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.490
I said I was going to do.

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:20.110
You begin to build this reputation.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:22.460
If you're constantly being
influenced and moved by

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.050
what other people think about you,

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:27.170
it means there's a deficiency
in what you think about you.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:32.170
And so the key is not some
esoteric belief system,

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.870
it's a pattern of keeping the
promises that you make to you.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.160
That's the groundwork of self-confidence.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.950
For sure and it is a pattern.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.800
When I meet people that
lack confidence, I think

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.020
let me serve you, let's
begin to keep the promises

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:44.900
you make to you.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.620
You're so worried about,
there's this addiction to other

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.820
people's approval in the world.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.653
- Right.
- Right?

00:07:49.653 --> 00:07:52.050
The greatest addiction
today, it used to be drugs.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.070
Before that it was alcohol.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.080
There's all these addictions,
sex addictions, whatever.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.990
The number one addiction
in the world today

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.850
is the addiction to
other people's approval

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.594
and that's because we
don't approve of ourselves

00:08:00.594 --> 00:08:03.880
or we don't feel a spirit, a universe,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.620
a God that we believe
in that approves of us.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.441
And so my confidence
comes from both my faith

00:08:08.441 --> 00:08:11.200
and in the fact that I keep
promises I make to myself.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.620
That's the groundwork of all confidence.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.930
- Rule number seven, max out your life.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.450
- See at the end of my
life, the Lord's going to go

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.570
hey by the way, this guy over here,

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.350
this is the man you could have been.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.010
This is the person you were born to be.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.060
This would have been your dreams.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.800
This is where you would have
gone, what you would have seen,

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.750
who you would've helped,
what you would've changed.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.900
This would've been your book.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:30.790
Meet him.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.770
My dream in my life is that
when I meet that person

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.000
we're not total strangers.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.630
You don't want to get
to the end of your life

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:39.620
and that character is a
total stranger to you.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.500
You know damn well there's
going to be a funeral

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.420
for you some day.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.950
At that funeral, there's going
to be a sense and a spirit

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.090
of what you could have become.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.620
The woman, the man you could
have become and every day

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:51.030
those decisions you're
making to max out your life

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.160
are chasing that person.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.710
See you know what I want
at the end of my life

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:55.543
when I meet him?

00:08:55.543 --> 00:08:56.840
I want to be identical twins.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.300
Ted and Ed are going to meet
each other some day and I'm

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.503
going to say hey man, good to see you.

00:09:00.503 --> 00:09:01.820
